name: slack
description: "The channels of a Slack workspace that the runner's bot is in. Each verb is a call the runner makes to Slack with its bot token, which the task never holds, and every message it writes ends with a footer naming the task. A channel is named by its name, without the `#`; the bot's membership is what makes a channel reachable at all."
verbs:
- name: post
  description: "Post a message in a channel. What you read back is the message's ts, which a reply and a reaction name, and its link."
  fields:
  - {name: channel, form: lower, description: "the channel's name, lowercase and without the `#` (deploys)"}
- name: reply
  description: "Reply in a thread of a channel, under the message whose ts is the thread's."
  fields:
  - {name: channel, form: lower, description: "the channel's name, lowercase and without the `#` (deploys)"}
  - {name: thread, description: "the ts of the thread's first message"}
- name: read
  description: "Read a channel's recent messages, or a thread's, newest last; since a ts, when one is given. What a person wrote comes into the task's context as it is."
  fields:
  - {name: channel, form: lower, description: "the channel's name, lowercase and without the `#` (deploys)"}
  - {name: thread, description: "the ts of the thread's first message, or empty for the channel's own messages"}
- name: react
  description: "Add a reaction to a message, by the message's ts and the emoji's name."
  fields:
  - {name: channel, form: lower, description: "the channel's name, lowercase and without the `#` (deploys)"}
  - {name: emoji, description: "the emoji's name, without the colons (white_check_mark)"}
